                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 6.0, 67.0, 317.0, 261.0 ],
                                                    "text": "post processing FX pass that generates a smear / trail FX.\n\nit works with 3d objects against the empty background\n\nthe lower the alpha the longer the trail\n\nit needs the ste.3dWorld erase_color to have opacity at 0.\n\nit is a pass, you place it in your patch and it will automatically effect the look of the final render, you don't need to connect it to anything as it automatically couples with the 3dWorld\n\nif you want to have more \"pass\" effects\nyou chain them connecting the 2nd outlet of the jit.gl.pass with the first inlet of the following jit.gl.pass\n\ncheck the helpfile of the jit.gl.pass for more info"
                                                }
                                            },
